    <item>
      <title>Derivative Calculator</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/works/apps/derivative-calculator/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 15 Nov 2016 00:00:00 -0300</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/works/apps/derivative-calculator/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This app calculates the derivative of a function for you. It parses the input into a tree of operators, numbers and variables, passes through the tree deriving the functions and then transforms it back to LaTeX, so the result can be shown.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is not optmized, so you may have to do some algebraic manipulations to simplify the result.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;link rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; type=&#34;text/css&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/css/derivative.css&#34; /&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;function&#34;&gt;Function&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;inputBorder&#34;&gt;
  &lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; id=&#34;formInput&#34;/&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;variable&#34;&gt;Variable&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;inputBorder&#34;&gt;
  &lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; id=&#34;varInput&#34;/&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;input id=&#34;calc&#34; type=&#34;submit&#34; value=&#34;Calculate&#34; onclick=&#34;main()&#34;/&gt;
&lt;script&gt;
  var a = function(e) {
    if (e.keyCode == 13)
      document.getElementById(&#39;calc&#39;).click();
  }
  document.getElementById(&#39;formInput&#39;).onkeypress = a
  document.getElementById(&#39;varInput&#39;).onkeypress = a
&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;p id=&#34;result&#34; class=&#34;output&#34;&gt;..........&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    
